{"shortDescription":"Central European currencies were mostly higher on Monday after weakening last week, with inflation data from Poland pointing to stable interest rates this year.","astDescription":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Central European currencies were mostly higher on Monday after weakening last week, with inflation data from Poland pointing to stable interest rates this year."]},{"type":"list","children":[{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Poland's gross domestic product (GDP) grew by 3.9% in the second quarter from a year earlier, slightly stronger than estimated earlier, with analysts saying the data showed that the Polish economy proved resilient to the crisis in the Middle East and higher crude prices."]}]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["However, Polish inflation rose to 3.4% in August while analysts had expected it to edge up to 3.1% from 3.0% in July, cooling expectations for interest rate cuts this year."]}]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["\"The most concerning factor is core inflation, which has risen to around 3.2–3.3% year-on-year. We'll have to wait for details, but fuel-sensitive categories likely still play a significant role. There will be no interest rate cuts in September or until the end of the year,\" Pekao BP analysts wrote in a comment on social media platform X."]}]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Poland's Monetary Policy Council (MPC) will meet next week to decide on interest rates."]}]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["After its last meeting in July, central bank Governor Adam Glapinski said he could propose a 25-basis-point interest rate cut after the summer, but analysts said other members could prove more cautious about further monetary easing."]}]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["The Polish zloty ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"OANDA:EURPLN","text":"OANDA:EURPLN"}}," rose 0.2% to 4.3310 per euro at 0822 GMT."]}]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["\"For the remainder of the week, the (zloty) will remain primarily influenced by the external environment. We assume that the impact of regional geopolitical risks will weaken, and investors' attention will shift to changes in oil prices and the performance of the dollar,\" PKO BP said."]}]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["\"The balance of opportunities and risks for the zloty remains slightly negative, so we expect the EUR/PLN to test the 4.34–4.35 resistance zone and the USD/PLN to rise towards 3.76–3.77 within the week.\""]}]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Elsewhere, the Czech crown ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"OANDA:EURCZK","text":"OANDA:EURCZK"}}," was stable at 24.1240 per euro while the Hungarian forint ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"FX:EURHUF","text":"FX:EURHUF"}}," rose 0.3% to 364.25."]}]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Shares on the Warsaw stock exchange ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"GPW:GPW","text":"GPW:GPW"}}," gained 0.8% but other bourses in the region were down, with Bucharest ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"BVB:BET","text":"BVB:BET"}}," falling 1.5%."]}]}]},{"type":"table","children":[{"type":"table-body","children":[{"type":"table-row","children":[{"type":"table-data-cell","params":{"colspan":3},"children":[{"type":"p","children":["CEE MARKETS SNAPSHOT AT  1022 CET"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[]},{"type":"table-data-cell","params":{"hidden":true}},{"type":"table-data-cell","params":{"hidden":true}}]},{"type":"table-row","children":[{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["CURRENCIES"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Latest trade"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Previous close"